{
  "info": {
    "name": "Extra Requirements Demo",
    "description": "A short, linear walk through the extra requirements, for a demo video of about 2 minutes. Send the requests from top to bottom, or run the collection with the Collection Runner. Use the \"Co-working Space Reservation - Local\" environment for {{URL}}.\n\nRun `npm run demo:reset` before each run. The reset deletes the users named Demo Admin, Demo Alice and Demo Bob, and the demo space, so \"0. Setup\" can register them again. Send \"0. Setup\" before you record.\n\nEach request name starts with a 4-digit number in the run order. Most names then give the actor: Admin, Alice or Bob. A name with no actor is a public request. The collection keeps one token for each actor, so you never log in or log out between requests.\n\nA name that ends with (Email) makes the server send an email. The force closure emails Alice. The admin edit and the admin delete each email Bob. The admin delete also gives Alice a reservation from the waitlist, which emails Alice.\n\nTo show the emails in real inboxes, set the collection variables adminEmail, aliceEmail and bobEmail to real addresses. Gmail plus-addresses (you+alice@gmail.com, you+bob@gmail.com) put all the emails into one inbox. The server must have SMTP_HOST set to send the emails. Without it, the server console shows each email.\n\n\"0005\" makes a reservation that ends 4 seconds later. A reservation must start and end on the same day, so do not send \"0. Setup\" within a few seconds of midnight Bangkok time.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "noauth"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "adminEmail",
      "value": "demo-admin@coworking.test",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "aliceEmail",
      "value": "demo-alice@coworking.test",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "bobEmail",
      "value": "demo-bob@coworking.test",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0. Setup",
      "description": "Send these before you record. Run `npm run demo:reset` first. The last request makes a reservation for Alice that ends 4 seconds later.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "0001 Admin Registers",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// The demo days, 1 and 2 days from now (Bangkok time)",
                  "const bkkDay = (n) => new Date(Date.now() + 7 * 3600e3 + n * 86400e3).toISOString().slice(0, 10);",
                  "[1, 2].forEach((n) => pm.collectionVariables.set(\"day\" + n, bkkDay(n)));"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status code is 201\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"adminToken\", pm.response.json().token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{URL}}/api/v1/auth/register",
              "host": [
                "{{URL}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "register"
              ]
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Demo Admin\",\n  \"tel\": \"02-218-6000\",\n  \"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"admin1234\",\n  \"role\": \"admin\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
